                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 420.0, 380.0, 130.0, 35.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Lower feedback when pitch is 0 semi-tones"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "background": 1,
                                                    "id": "obj-103",
                                                    "linecount": 5,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 40.0, 50.0, 484.0, 78.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Sets the amount of processed audio to be sent back to the reverberator. In the case of sounds that have a transposition of 0 semi-tones, the feedback loop may produce loud digital \"larsens\" with long reverb tail and delay time. To prevent this to happen too often, the sound is low-passed then high-passed, and slightly shifted in frequency. Additionally, a noise gate prevents long reverb/delay tails to remain audible for (almost) ever."
                                                }
                                            },
