                                    "patching_rect": [ 280.0, 177.0, 77.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "External LFO"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-73",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 97.0, 251.0, 93.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "LFO subpatcher"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-42",
                                    "linecount": 8,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 440.0, 215.0, 122.0 ],
                                    "text": "The range of delay modulation is controlled by the Depth parameter. \nThe value of Depth is used to transform the range of the triangular modulation into a delay time modulation. The modulation is then smoothed and translated to samples before feeding the delay~ object."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-59",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 325.0, 220.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "To obtain stereo modulation, we’re shifting the input phase of the triangle~ object whose waveform is used to control the delay of the right audio channel. The phase offset between L and R modulation waveforms is controlled by the Spread parameter."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-67",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 270.0, 210.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "The triangular waveform is then used to increase and decrease the amount of delay applied to the input signal. "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-69",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 670.0, 160.0, 202.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "The phasor~ object generates a signal ramp, at a rate controlled by the Rate parameter. The rate can be set by tempo tapping. The ramp is used as a phase value (x) to read in a triangular wavetable stored in the triangle~ object (y). "
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "fontname": "Lato Bold",
                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                    "id": "obj-96",
